flowchart TB
STATUS["ARIA v1.1 — UNIFIED PROPOSED ARCHITECTURE
Shared principles across operating and builder systems
Not proof of implementation, acceptance, deployment, or permission
Foundations drawn from CLAUDE.md Laws 1–21 + VISION.md + LESSONS.md"]
HUMAN["TIER 0 — BRAD / AUTHORIZED HUMAN OWNER<br/>Law 1: socio-economic status is priority #1<br/>Outcomes, standards, grants, reserved decisions<br/>Amend, approve, suspend, revoke, stop"]
POLICY["TIER 1 — CONSTITUTION AND VERSIONED POLICY<br/>Law 21: every change advances a named section of VISION.md<br/>Safety → welfare / privacy / consent / human rights<br/>→ integrity → security → resources → efficiency → optimization"]
STATUS -.-> HUMAN
HUMAN -->|Approves applicable policy and grants| POLICY

subgraph COMMON["COMMON GROUND — APPLIES TO EVERY TIER AND BOTH ORGANIZATIONS"]
    direction TB
    PRINCIPLES["SAME CONCEPTS, SCOPED TO EACH RESPONSIBILITY<br/>Authority: explicit purpose, permitted data, actions, audience, expiry<br/>Evidence (Laws 2, 3, 19): exact identity, provenance, time, coverage, uncertainty, corrections<br/>Measure do not recall; absence reported as absence; indexed ≠ aware<br/>Responsibility: owner, intended outcome, dependencies, next action, release conditions<br/>Resources: reservations, aggregate exposure, budgets, exclusive ownership<br/>Execution (Laws 8, 9, 17): durable intent, stable IDs, bounded retry, unknown-effect reconciliation<br/>Landed ≠ live; listener judges outcome, not attempt<br/>Assurance (Laws 10, 20): independent claim-specific verification, soundness AND progress<br/>Red-proofed gates; every repair states falsifiable prediction; fix the CLASS<br/>Continuity: checkpoints, restart reconciliation, handoff, retention and deletion<br/>Learning: proportionate proposals, validation, authorized change, rollback / retirement"]
    CONTRACT["RECURSIVE CONTRACT — EVERY CHILD INHERITS THE BOUNDARY<br/>Same or narrower data, authority, audience, expiry, and budget<br/>Explicit tools, allowed effects, stop rules, evidence, receipts, and handoff<br/>Parent responsibility remains accountable<br/>Cannot check a required invariant? Do not dispatch"]
    PRINCIPLES --> CONTRACT
end

ENFORCE["INDEPENDENT POLICY / EXECUTION CONTROL PLANE<br/>Identity, credentials, scoped permissions, revocation<br/>Network / filesystem / provider / device boundaries<br/>Budgets, reservations, expiry, audit IDs, stop controls<br/>Recheck current authority at dispatch, retry, resumption, and effects<br/>Laws 4–7, 11–16, 18 enforced here (readiness, health numbers, enumeration, smokes, unkeyed rows, critical escalation, backups, monitors that cry wolf, warnings fail suite)"]
POLICY --> ENFORCE
POLICY -.->|Defines applicable constraints| COMMON
COMMON -.-> ENFORCE

subgraph OPERATING["OPERATING ORGANIZATION — CARRY HUMAN RESPONSIBILITIES"]
    direction TB
    OC["TIER 2 — ARIA RESPONSIBILITY COORDINATOR<br/>Shared understanding, source health, evidence, uncertainty<br/>Plans and continuing follow-through"]
    OR["TIER 3 — OWNED RESPONSIBILITIES AND CAPABILITY LANES<br/>Home / energy / permitted sensing; communications<br/>Business / finance; projects / research; public presence; platform"]
    OW["TIER 4 — BOUNDED WORK PACKAGES / WORKERS<br/>Scoped parent grant; current dependencies; assigned outcome"]
    OD["TIER 5 — ACTION INTENT / OUTBOX / DISPATCH<br/>Stable action and attempt IDs; idempotency where supported<br/>No blind duplicate after an uncertain effect"]
    OA["SCOPED PROVIDER OR PHYSICAL ADAPTER<br/>Actual live-enabled state requires current evidence"]
    OV["INDEPENDENT OUTCOME AND SIDE-EFFECT CHECK<br/>Acknowledgement is not observed completion<br/>Law 20: falsifiable prediction checked by listener"]
    ACCOUNT["RESPONSIBILITY ACCOUNT<br/>Established result, failed / unresolved / not run / refused checks<br/>Owned next action, reconsideration, completion, or reserved decision"]
    OC --> OR --> OW --> OD --> OA --> OV --> ACCOUNT
end

subgraph BUILDERS["TEMPORARY BUILDER ORGANIZATION — BUILD AND REPAIR ARIA"]
    direction TB
    BC["TIER 2 — BUILD COORDINATOR<br/>Ready queue, dependency/resource graph, consolidated owner account"]
    BG["TIER 3 — CONTRACT STEWARD AND DOMAIN GOVERNORS<br/>Foundation; responsibility; protection; operations; capability integration<br/>Version shared meaning and preserve existing candidates"]
    BP["TIER 4 — READY BOUNDED PACKAGES<br/>G01–G28 current recheck / acceptance work<br/>Exact baseline, dependencies, file/resource lease, budget, reviewer<br/>Parallel only when independently ready and non-conflicting"]
    BI["TIER 5 — ISOLATED IMPLEMENTATION AND AUTHOR CHECKS<br/>One writer per file across branches and worktrees<br/>Containment proven before executable tests; no self-certification"]
    BR["INDEPENDENT EXACT-ARTIFACT REVIEW<br/>PASS for specified scope / FAIL / BLOCKED / UNKNOWN<br/>Author receipt or source presence is not independent effect proof<br/>Law 10: red-proof the gate"]
    BQ["SINGLE INTEGRATION / RELEASE QUEUE<br/>Designated integrator; compatible dependencies and migrations<br/>Combined acceptance and complete responsibility rehearsal"]
    BL["SPECIFICALLY APPROVED ROLLOUT / RECOVERY<br/>Designated operator; current release limits<br/>Verify loaded identity THEN original intended outcome<br/>Laws 8 & 9: landed by bytes, boot == HEAD"]
    BC --> BG --> BP --> BI --> BR --> BQ --> BL
end

ENFORCE --> OC
ENFORCE --> BC
COMMON -.-> OPERATING
COMMON -.-> BUILDERS

subgraph CROSSCUT["CROSS-CUTTING SYSTEMS — SCOPED ACCESS, NOT UNIVERSAL VISIBILITY"]
    direction TB
    RECORD["DURABLE RECORDS AND VERSIONED CONTRACTS<br/>Identity; source results; evidence / claims; responsibilities<br/>Reservations; attempts; verification; disclosure / account outputs<br/>Exact source / config / candidate / loaded-build bindings<br/>Operating ledger AND builder registry use these semantics<br/>Reuse existing stores; shared semantics do not require one database"]
    ASSURE["INDEPENDENT ASSURANCE MESH<br/>Compliance / privacy / disclosure; evidence and decision quality<br/>Outcomes and side effects; sampled adversarial inspection<br/>System health; investigations; oversight-quality review<br/>Scoped budgets and access; no agent approves its own authority"]
    LEARN["CONTROLLED LEARNING / RELEASE + CLASS-CLOSURE LOOP<br/>Law 20 explicit:<br/>1. Measure (Law 2) with the command that produced the number<br/>2. Error found → investigate and classify (LESSONS.md family of shapes)<br/>3. Fix the ROOT-CAUSE CLASS with a mechanical gate, not only the instance<br/>4. Verify the entire class is closed (red-proof, prediction held, class does not reappear)<br/>5. Closed class becomes a new ongoing measurement<br/>6. Cycle continues<br/>Observe → assess → propose → independently validate<br/>→ obtain applicable approval → rollout → monitor → revise / retire<br/>Validated repairs return as bounded builder proposals<br/>Approved releases update ARIA; no implicit authority expansion<br/>Policy or mandate changes return to the authorized human<br/>Reliability never automatically expands autonomy"]
end

COMMON -.-> RECORD
COMMON -.-> ASSURE
COMMON -.-> LEARN
ASSURE -.->|Independent operating checks| OV
ASSURE -.->|Independent builder checks| BR
ACCOUNT -->|Outcome evidence and unresolved causes| LEARN
BL -->|Exact-artifact and original-outcome evidence| LEARN
LEARN -->|New measurement after class closed| ASSURE

STOP["UNIVERSAL FAIL-CLOSED / ESCALATION RULE<br/>Missing authority, unchecked invariant, failed isolation, drift,<br/>conflicting lease, exceeded budget, unsafe or uncertain effect:<br/>stop or contain the affected work; preserve evidence; reconcile<br/>Continue unrelated authorized work; return genuinely reserved decisions<br/>Reserved matters return to human with evidence, options, recommendation<br/>Silence is never approval; owner is not the routine message bus"]
HUMAN -->|Independent stop / revocation| ENFORCE
CONTRACT -.-> STOP
ASSURE -.-> STOP

